{"kind":"artifact","text":"AGENTS.md at head fe7349ff, on current main: the quiet-wave gate can now reach zero, and stale is distinguished from retired.\n\nSuccessor to 0d040b71, closing both blockers review raised against 85e5dbb2, and published on current main c0f3533d rather than one world behind it.\n\nThe approved-head loop counted every ratified approval, stale and retired included. `gs merge` refuses those, so a head held up by one is not waiting for a merger but for a fresh review, and waiting longer never clears it. An unreachable precondition is the one failure a gate on an irreversible step cannot have: it either blocks for ever or teaches the operator to bypass it. Filtering removes the stale approval of bc469129 and keeps the genuinely outstanding 00b7070d.\n\nThe second finding is the one worth recording, because I made the mistake this page exists to prevent. I reported the path clear after retiring five artifacts, and three remained: stale, but not retired. Live means not retired. Stale says a basis underneath the artifact moved; it does not say the pointer was withdrawn, so a stale artifact still occupies its path and is still a predecessor a successor must retire. Both render as \"not the current one\" to a reader looking for what is current, which is what makes them easy to conflate. The page now says so where the retire rule is stated.\n\nThis retires four predecessors at AGENTS.md: 0d040b71, and the three that were stale rather than retired — bc50ab8c, 6a1a70b6 and 3cf0259f. All mine.\n\nGates at this head: `go vet ./...` clean, `git diff --check` clean, `go test ./internal/docset -count=1` passes in 111.0s, clean worktree, and current main is a parent.","body":{"commit":"fe7349ffbc0a254139b4afb4432d6c230f591830","path":"AGENTS.md"}}